/*!
    \class QRect
    \brief Defines a rectangle using \c{integer} precision.

    The QRect class defines a rectangle in the plane using integer
    coordinates for the top-left corner, width, and height.

    \note The \c{isValid()} method returns \c{false} for a null rectangle.

    \warning Calling \c{setWidth()} with a negative value produces undefined behaviour.

    \section1 Getting the dimensions

    Use width() and height() to get the dimensions of the rectangle.

    \section2 Related classes

    See also QSize and QPoint.
*/
